// BL-82 EM-5.9 (T56.30) — rotating gameplay tips shown on the connecting /
// loading screen. Data-driven (edit here, no recompile). A random entry is
// picked each time the loading screen appears.
//
// Keep tips short (one line), spoiler-free, and true of the CURRENT build —
// a tip that promises a feature the client can't do yet is worse than none.
// Plain `Vec<String>`, so RON is just a list of strings.
[
    "Press 'L' to see all default key bindings.",
    "Type /say or /s to chat only with players right around you.",
    "Type /region or /r to chat with players a couple hundred blocks away.",
    "Type /group or /g to chat only with your current group.",
    "Send a private message with /tell followed by a player name.",
    "Keep an eye out for food, chests and other loot spread across the world.",
    "Inventory full of raw food? Try crafting better meals from it.",
    "Open the map to find dungeons and points of interest worth exploring.",
    "Adjust the graphics for your machine in the Esc menu if things run slow.",
    "Press the social key to see who else is online.",
    "Sit near a campfire to slowly recover from your injuries.",
    "Roll to move faster and dodge incoming attacks.",
    "Open the crafting menu to build better bags, armour and tools.",
    "Xindeler is early, pre-alpha software — expect rough edges, and thanks for playing!",
    "Your class shapes your playstyle: spend skill points in the character diary.",
    "Drag an ability from the diary onto your hotbar to bind it to a key.",
]
